Subject: [PATCH] Attract mode keeps rolling through the games

Attract mode only moves the list while the list stands still, and the "attract" event it sends every
frame cleared the list's idle flag (upstream "Cache idle state" change). So attract moved one game
and then sat on it until somebody pressed a button. The per-frame attract event no longer clears it.
---
diff --git a/RetroFE/Source/Graphics/Page.cpp b/RetroFE/Source/Graphics/Page.cpp
index 7c87b283..c72acefe 100644
--- a/RetroFE/Source/Graphics/Page.cpp
+++ b/RetroFE/Source/Graphics/Page.cpp
@@ -618,7 +618,9 @@ void Page::triggerEventOnAllMenus(const std::string& event) {
 				component->triggerEvent(event, index);
 		}
 	}
-	invalidateIdleCache();
+	// ArcadeMaster: "attract" is sent every frame while attract mode runs. Clearing the idle cache for it meant attract
+	// never saw the list standing still: it moved one game and then sat there for good (RACE2, 2026-11-26)
+	if (event != "attract") invalidateIdleCache();
 }
 
 
